{"products":[{"id":8607339511842,"title":"COLOMBIA - EL PUENTE , NATURAL","handle":"colombia-el-puente-natural","body_html":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRegion:\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePalestina, Huila – Colombia\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAltitude:\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e1.680 m.a.s.l\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eVarieties:\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eCaturra – Colombia – Castillo – Bourbon\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDrying:\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eParabolic dryer\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eProcessing:\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eNatural\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNotes:\u003cbr\u003e\u003c\/strong\u003eCocao, Figs, Red Apple \u0026amp; Raspberry\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSCA Score: \u0026gt;86\u003cbr\u003e\u003cmeta charset=\"utf-8\"\u003e\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEl Puente Mill, built in 2018, is a central processing facility in the Palestina region of Huila, Colombia. Named after a nearby footbridge, it serves over 100 small-scale farming families who deliver their coffee cherries for processing. Designed to handle larger volumes than individual farm mills, El Puente enables producers with limited resources to sell their coffee at premium prices, even before processing.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe project, led by renowned coffee expert Elkin Guzman, focuses on supporting farmers with limited infrastructure, motivating them to produce high-quality coffee while reducing processing risks. This initiative has significantly improved the livelihoods of local producers.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c\/p\u003e","published_at":"2026-09-02T10:46:57+02:00","created_at":"2026-08-25T10:42:43+02:00","updated_at":"2026-09-08T20:34:37+02:00","vendor":"Sorcery Coffee Roasters","product_type":"","tags":[],"variants":[{"id":46548964343842,"title":"250GR","option1":"250GR","option2":null,"option3":null,"sku":null,"requires_shipping":true,"taxable":true,"featured_image":null,"available":true,"price":"390.00","grams":0,"compare_at_price":null,"position":1,"product_id":8607339511842,"created_at":"2026-08-25T10:46:30+02:00","updated_at":"2026-09-08T20:34:37+02:00"}],"images":[{"id":41459087933474,"created_at":"2026-09-02T10:45:37+02:00","position":1,"updated_at":"2026-09-02T10:45:38+02:00","product_id":8607339511842,"variant_ids":[],"src":"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0570\/5138\/1794\/files\/Sorcery_labels_80_x_80_mm_1_.pdf.pdf_1_.pdf_12.png?v=1788338738","width":302,"height":302},{"id":41213124083746,"created_at":"2026-08-25T10:45:47+02:00","position":2,"updated_at":"2026-08-25T10:45:49+02:00","product_id":8607339511842,"variant_ids":[],"src":"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0570\/5138\/1794\/files\/148919605_2852123478359985_2075410698724060687_o.jpg?v=1787647549","width":1440,"height":1785},{"id":41213124116514,"created_at":"2026-08-25T10:45:47+02:00","position":3,"updated_at":"2026-08-25T10:45:49+02:00","product_id":8607339511842,"variant_ids":[],"src":"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0570\/5138\/1794\/files\/20210627_151151157_iOS_edited.jpg?v=1787647549","width":1025,"height":1366}],"options":[{"name":"SIZE","position":1,"values":["250GR"]}]},{"id":8607338889250,"title":"COLOMBIA - EL PUENTE, HONEY","handle":"colombia-el-puente-honey","body_html":"\u003cdiv class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-42fcf11 elementor-widget elementor-widget-woocommerce-product-content\"\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRegion:\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePalestina, Huila – Colombia\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAltitude:\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e1.550 – 1.980 m.a.s.l\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eVarieties:\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eCastillo – Caturra – Colombia – Bourbon\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDrying:\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eSun-dried\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eProcessing:\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHoney\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNotes:\u003cbr\u003e\u003c\/strong\u003eHoney, Mint, Panela, Sugar Cane \u0026amp; Sweet Lime\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSCA Score: \u0026gt;86\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003c\/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c0ca645 elementor-widget elementor-widget-button\"\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\u003cmeta charset=\"utf-8\"\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEl Puente Mill, built in 2018, is a central processing facility in the Palestina region of Huila, Colombia. Named after a nearby footbridge, it serves over 100 small-scale farming families who deliver their coffee cherries for processing. Designed to handle larger volumes than individual farm mills, El Puente enables producers with limited resources to sell their coffee at premium prices, even before processing.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe project, led by renowned coffee expert Elkin Guzman, focuses on supporting farmers with limited infrastructure, motivating them to produce high-quality coffee while reducing processing risks. This initiative has significantly improved the livelihoods of local producers.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003c\/div\u003e","published_at":"2026-09-07T14:58:54+02:00","created_at":"2026-08-25T10:42:11+02:00","updated_at":"2026-09-08T20:34:37+02:00","vendor":"Sorcery Coffee Roasters","product_type":"","tags":[],"variants":[{"id":46548960411682,"title":"250GR","option1":"250GR","option2":null,"option3":null,"sku":null,"requires_shipping":true,"taxable":true,"featured_image":null,"available":true,"price":"240.00","grams":0,"compare_at_price":null,"position":1,"product_id":8607338889250,"created_at":"2026-08-25T10:42:11+02:00","updated_at":"2026-09-08T20:34:37+02:00"}],"images":[{"id":41212657270818,"created_at":"2026-08-25T10:21:33+02:00","position":1,"updated_at":"2026-08-25T10:21:34+02:00","product_id":8607338889250,"variant_ids":[],"src":"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0570\/5138\/1794\/files\/Sorcery_labels_80_x_80_mm_1_.pdf.pdf_1_.pdf_10.png?v=1787646094","width":302,"height":302},{"id":41212649275426,"created_at":"2026-08-25T10:20:57+02:00","position":2,"updated_at":"2026-08-25T10:20:59+02:00","product_id":8607338889250,"variant_ids":[],"src":"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0570\/5138\/1794\/files\/ELP.jpg?v=1787646059","width":640,"height":800},{"id":41212649308194,"created_at":"2026-08-25T10:20:57+02:00","position":3,"updated_at":"2026-08-25T10:20:59+02:00","product_id":8607338889250,"variant_ids":[],"src":"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0570\/5138\/1794\/files\/ELPH.jpg?v=1787646059","width":1440,"height":1785}],"options":[{"name":"SIZE","position":1,"values":["250GR"]}]},{"id":7918217363490,"title":"COLOMBIA - MAYPOP","handle":"colombia-maypop","body_html":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCOLOMBIA\u003cbr\u003eREGION:\u003c\/strong\u003e RISARALDA\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFARM:\u003c\/strong\u003e FINCA MILAN\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePRODUCER \u003c\/strong\u003e: JULIO MADRID\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eALTITUDE:\u003c\/strong\u003e 1.400 m.a.s.l\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eVARIETY:\u003c\/strong\u003e CATURRA\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDRYING: SOLAR\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePROCESSING:\u003c\/strong\u003e WASHED \u0026amp; CULTURED\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGREEN SCORE\u003c\/strong\u003e : 86\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNOTES: Passionfruit, Floral, Peach, Candy like \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cmeta charset=\"utf-8\"\u003e \u003cstrong data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"15\"\u003eFinca Milan\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003cspan\u003e is located in the village of El Hogar in the municipality of Pereira, Risaralda, Colombia, and is owned by third-generation coffee producer \u003c\/span\u003e\u003cstrong data-start=\"156\" data-end=\"197\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"whitespace-normal\"\u003eJulio Cesar Madrid\u003c\/span\u003e\u003c\/span\u003e\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003cspan\u003e. Owned by the Madrid family for over 40 years, the 50-hectare farm combines tradition and innovation, producing specialty coffees using advanced fermentation methods such as Natural, Washed, Honey, and Culturing to create distinctive, high-quality cup profiles.\u003c\/span\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cmeta charset=\"utf-8\"\u003e \u003cspan\u003eCulturing Process: Coffee is fermented using a starter culture of yeasts and bacteria combined with locally sourced fruits and ingredients such as Passiflora (Passion fruit, Gulupa, Curuba), and panela from sugar cane. This controlled mixed fermentation enhances microbial activity, developing complex flavours and a distinctive specialty coffee profile\u003c\/span\u003e\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003c\/p\u003e","published_at":"2026-06-08T13:10:30+02:00","created_at":"2025-02-28T10:01:11+02:00","updated_at":"2026-09-08T20:34:37+02:00","vendor":"Sorcery Coffee Roasters","product_type":"","tags":[],"variants":[{"id":43557603967010,"title":"250GR","option1":"250GR","option2":null,"option3":null,"sku":"","requires_shipping":true,"taxable":true,"featured_image":null,"available":true,"price":"590.00","grams":0,"compare_at_price":null,"position":1,"product_id":7918217363490,"created_at":"2025-02-28T10:20:32+02:00","updated_at":"2026-09-08T20:34:37+02:00"}],"images":[{"id":40084813348898,"created_at":"2026-06-08T13:10:25+02:00","position":1,"updated_at":"2026-06-08T13:10:26+02:00","product_id":7918217363490,"variant_ids":[],"src":"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0570\/5138\/1794\/files\/Sorcerylabels_80x80mm_1_.pdf.pdf_1_.pdf_9.png?v=1780917026","width":302,"height":302}],"options":[{"name":"SIZE","position":1,"values":["250GR"]}]},{"id":7964650962978,"title":"COLOMBIA - PURPLE CATURRA SANGRIA","handle":"colombia-purple-caturra-sangria","body_html":"\u003ch3\u003ePurple Caturra – Bourbon Sangria Washed\u003c\/h3\u003e\n\u003ch4\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c\/h4\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRegion:\u003c\/strong\u003e Pitalito, Huila – Colombia\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFarm:\u003c\/strong\u003e El Eden\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAltitude:\u003c\/strong\u003e 1.500 m.a.s.l\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eVarieties:\u003c\/strong\u003e Purple Caturra \u0026amp; Bourbon\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDrying:\u003c\/strong\u003e Sun Drying\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eProcessing:\u003c\/strong\u003e Washed\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFermentation:\u003c\/strong\u003e Co-Fermentation\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNotes: Fanta Grape, Grapetizer , Peach, Jasmine \u003c\/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSCA Green Score: \u0026gt;88\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003eFarm Info\u003c\/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFinca El Edén, owned by\u003cspan\u003e \u003c\/span\u003e\u003ca rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https:\/\/www.sabores.co.za\/2021\/03\/08\/rodrigo-sanchez\/\" target=\"_blank\"\u003eRodrigo Sanchez\u003c\/a\u003e, is located in the Samaria district of Palestina at 1,500 MASL. The farm’s ideal climate, with over 8 hours of sunlight and annual rainfall between 1,800–2,000mm, supports cultivating high-quality varieties like Pink Bourbon and Purple Caturra. Harvests occur year-round, with peak seasons in October–December and a secondary harvest in May–June.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003ch4\u003e\n\u003cmeta charset=\"utf-8\"\u003e \u003cspan\u003eThe coffee cherries are carefully selected and floated to remove impurities before being evaluated for optimal Brix levels. \u003cbr\u003eSelected micro-organisms, including Lactobacillus and Saccharomyces cerevisiae, are cultivated and combined with red fruit juices to create a mother culture used for fermentation. \u003cbr\u003eThe cherries then undergo a controlled 190-hour fermentation, with Brix levels maintained above 6 and pH above 4 to enhance vibrant fruit notes while preserving the coffee’s natural character.\u003c\/span\u003e\n\u003c\/h4\u003e","published_at":"2026-06-08T13:08:23+02:00","created_at":"2025-05-14T09:52:09+02:00","updated_at":"2026-09-08T20:34:37+02:00","vendor":"Sorcery Coffee Roasters","product_type":"","tags":[],"variants":[{"id":43844429807650,"title":"250GR","option1":"250GR","option2":null,"option3":null,"sku":"","requires_shipping":true,"taxable":true,"featured_image":null,"available":true,"price":"590.00","grams":0,"compare_at_price":null,"position":1,"product_id":7964650962978,"created_at":"2025-05-27T17:43:34+02:00","updated_at":"2026-09-08T20:34:37+02:00"}],"images":[{"id":35381615067170,"created_at":"2025-05-27T17:43:17+02:00","position":1,"updated_at":"2025-05-27T17:43:25+02:00","product_id":7964650962978,"variant_ids":[],"src":"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0570\/5138\/1794\/files\/Sorcery_labels_80_x_80_mm_1_.pdf.pdf_1_.pdf_5.png?v=1748360605","width":302,"height":302},{"id":35274589962274,"created_at":"2025-05-14T09:51:38+02:00","position":2,"updated_at":"2025-05-27T17:43:25+02:00","product_id":7964650962978,"variant_ids":[],"src":"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0570\/5138\/1794\/files\/Sangria-2.jpg?v=1748360605","width":640,"height":800},{"id":35274590421026,"created_at":"2025-05-14T09:51:46+02:00","position":3,"updated_at":"2025-05-27T17:43:25+02:00","product_id":7964650962978,"variant_ids":[],"src":"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0570\/5138\/1794\/files\/20210626_222040587_iOS_edited.jpg?v=1748360605","width":1025,"height":1366}],"options":[{"name":"SIZE","position":1,"values":["250GR"]}]},{"id":8607340265506,"title":"COLOMBIA - TABI , WASHED","handle":"colombia-tabi-washed","body_html":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRegion:\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHuila – Colombia\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFarm | Producer\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eLas Flores | Jhoan Vergara\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAltitude:\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e1.780 m.a.s.l\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eVarieties:\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eTabi\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDrying:\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eCanopies\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFermentation:\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThermal Shock Submerged\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eProcessing:\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWashed\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNotes:\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eOolong tea, Floral, Rooibos with honey and lemon\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSCA Score: 87\u003cbr\u003e\u003cmeta charset=\"utf-8\"\u003e\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFinca Las Flores\u003c\/strong\u003e is a family-owned specialty coffee farm located in San Isidro, Acevedo, Huila, Colombia, at 1,750 MASL. Established in 1990 by Edilberto Vergara and Nubia Ayure, the 16-hectare farm has grown from just 2 hectares of coffee to full production, becoming a recognised producer of high-quality Colombian specialty coffee.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn 2006, the farm entered the Cup of Excellence, marking its transition from traditional coffee production to a focus on exceptional cup quality and specialty markets. Today, the second generation continues this legacy, investing in improved agricultural practices, varietal selection, and advanced processing methods tailored to Huila’s unique altitude and terroir.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFinca Las Flores is committed to innovation, traceability, and producing distinctive microlots that showcase the character and potential of Colombian specialty coffee.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c\/p\u003e","published_at":"2026-09-02T10:46:26+02:00","created_at":"2026-08-25T10:44:45+02:00","updated_at":"2026-09-08T20:34:37+02:00","vendor":"Sorcery Coffee Roasters","product_type":"","tags":[],"variants":[{"id":46548962279458,"title":"250GR","option1":"250GR","option2":null,"option3":null,"sku":null,"requires_shipping":true,"taxable":true,"featured_image":null,"available":true,"price":"550.00","grams":0,"compare_at_price":null,"position":1,"product_id":8607340265506,"created_at":"2026-08-25T10:44:45+02:00","updated_at":"2026-09-08T20:34:37+02:00"}],"images":[{"id":41459087736866,"created_at":"2026-09-02T10:45:34+02:00","position":1,"updated_at":"2026-09-02T10:45:35+02:00","product_id":8607340265506,"variant_ids":[],"src":"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0570\/5138\/1794\/files\/Sorcery_labels_80_x_80_mm_1_.pdf.pdf_1_.pdf_11.png?v=1788338735","width":302,"height":302},{"id":41213121921058,"created_at":"2026-08-25T10:44:37+02:00","position":2,"updated_at":"2026-08-25T10:44:38+02:00","product_id":8607340265506,"variant_ids":[],"src":"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0570\/5138\/1794\/files\/20240227_173043872_iOS_edited.jpg?v=1787647478","width":533,"height":800},{"id":41213121953826,"created_at":"2026-08-25T10:44:37+02:00","position":3,"updated_at":"2026-08-25T10:44:38+02:00","product_id":8607340265506,"variant_ids":[],"src":"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0570\/5138\/1794\/files\/Las-Flores.jpg?v=1787647478","width":1201,"height":1201}],"options":[{"name":"SIZE","position":1,"values":["250GR"]}]},{"id":8086978461730,"title":"Compostable Coffee Pods","handle":"compostable-coffee-pods","body_html":"\u003cdiv class=\"row\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"col-sm-9 xs-ac\"\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\n\u003cmeta charset=\"utf-8\"\u003e \u003cspan\u003e100% compostable Nespresso-style coffee pods \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c\/span\u003e\u003cmeta charset=\"utf-8\"\u003e\n\u003c\/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRegion:\u003c\/strong\u003e Eastern Cauca, Tierradentro – Colombia\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFarm:\u003c\/strong\u003e Several Smallholder Farms\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eVarieties:\u003c\/strong\u003e Caturra, Castillo and Colombia\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDrying:\u003c\/strong\u003e Parabolic Drying\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eProcessing:\u003c\/strong\u003e Washed\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNotes: CARAMEL, HONEY, VANILLA, VERY COMPLEX\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSCA Green Score: \u0026gt;85\u003c\/strong\u003e\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eComposting 4WKS At HomE\u003c\/h2\u003e\n\u003c\/div\u003e\n\u003c\/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"row\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"col-sm-12 xs-ac\"\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOur pods are certified home-compostable by OK Compost Home. Each home composting environment is unique, from worm farms to bokashi bins. The time your pods take to decompose will fluctuate depending on your method. Don’t worry, our pods will break down into soil. A little patience goes a long way 😉\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHere are our top tips to ensure your pods (pouch and all) will be food for the worms in no time!\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e- Our pods break down faster in hot composting environments.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e- Your compost heap should be at least half a cubic metre.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e- Throw your used pods in the middle of the heap (this is where it gets the hottest).\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e- Water your heap well.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e- Turn your compost often to introduce fresh oxygen.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e- Don’t panic if the coffee and veggie lid decompose quicker than the shell.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e- Let Nature do her thing. In roughly 3 months, your pods will become nutritious compost.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003c\/div\u003e\n\u003c\/div\u003e","published_at":"2025-10-06T09:31:30+02:00","created_at":"2025-10-06T09:31:28+02:00","updated_at":"2026-09-08T20:34:37+02:00","vendor":"Sorcery Coffee Roasters","product_type":"","tags":[],"variants":[{"id":44372124303394,"title":"10 X PODS","option1":"10 X PODS","option2":null,"option3":null,"sku":null,"requires_shipping":true,"taxable":true,"featured_image":null,"available":true,"price":"120.00","grams":0,"compare_at_price":null,"position":1,"product_id":8086978461730,"created_at":"2025-10-06T09:31:28+02:00","updated_at":"2026-09-08T20:34:37+02:00"}],"images":[{"id":36565041446946,"created_at":"2025-10-06T09:30:11+02:00","position":1,"updated_at":"2025-10-06T09:30:13+02:00","product_id":8086978461730,"variant_ids":[],"src":"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0570\/5138\/1794\/files\/IMG_2709.jpg?v=1759735813","width":1170,"height":1455}],"options":[{"name":"SIZE","position":1,"values":["10 X PODS"]}]},{"id":8209104928802,"title":"GUATEMALA - HUEHUETENANGO WASHED","handle":"guatemala-huehuetenango-washed","body_html":"\u003cdiv id=\"bgLayers_comp-m1tbe2fd\" data-hook=\"bgLayers\" data-motion-part=\"BG_LAYER comp-m1tbe2fd\" class=\"MW5IWV\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv id=\"bgMedia_comp-m1tbe2fd\" data-motion-part=\"BG_MEDIA comp-m1tbe2fd\" class=\"VgO9Yg\"\u003e\u003c\/div\u003e\n\u003c\/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv data-mesh-id=\"comp-m1tbe2fdinlineContent\" data-testid=\"inline-content\" class=\"\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv data-mesh-id=\"comp-m1tbe2fdinlineContent-gridContainer\" data-testid=\"mesh-container-content\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv id=\"comp-m1tbe2fd7\" class=\"Z_l5lU ku3DBC zQ9jDz qvSjx3 Vq6kJx comp-m1tbe2fd7 wixui-rich-text\" data-testid=\"richTextElement\"\u003e\n\u003ch1 class=\"font_0 wixui-rich-text__text\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"\u003eHUEHUETENANGO\u003c\/span\u003e\u003c\/h1\u003e\n\u003c\/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv id=\"comp-m1tbe2fe4\" class=\"Z_l5lU ku3DBC zQ9jDz qvSjx3 Vq6kJx comp-m1tbe2fe4 wixui-rich-text\" data-testid=\"richTextElement\"\u003e\n\u003cp class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\"\u003e \u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"\u003eProcess: Washed and dried on rooftops, small patios and tarps. \u003c\/span\u003e\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"\u003eVarietals: Bourbon, Catuai, Caturra, Pache\u003c\/span\u003e\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"\u003eAltitude: \u003c\/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"\u003e1200 - 2000 masl\u003c\/span\u003e\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"\u003eRegion: Huehuetenango, Western Guatemala\u003c\/span\u003e\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"\u003eProducer: \u003c\/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"\u003eVarious smallholder producers.\u003c\/span\u003e\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"\u003eHarvest Period: September to April\u003cspan\u003e \u003c\/span\u003e\u003c\/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"\u003e\u003c\/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"\u003e\u003c\/span\u003e\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"\u003eSCA score on arrival sample:\u003cspan\u003e \u003c\/span\u003e82.25\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c\/span\u003e\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\"\u003e\u003cmeta charset=\"utf-8\"\u003eHuehuetenango is both a large department (or state) and the eponymous capital city of that same department. While coee isn’t grown in the city of Huehuetenango, it is abundant in the high altitude mountains to the west and north of the city. This coee is fully processed by smallholder farmers who have around 1 hectare of land. Cherries are harvested ripe and then de-pulped usually by either manual or small-motored pulpers. This is then left to ferment overnight until the coee’s remaining mucilage has broken down. Washing is then carried out, usually in special - ised channels. The extreme remoteness of Huehuetenango virtually requires all producers to process their own coee. Fortunately, the region has an almost infinite number of rivers and streams, so amill can be placed just about anywhere. The washed parchment is always sun dried as the small holders don’t have access to mechanical driers. The drying takes advantage of every bit of flat, full sun space that can be found, which is limited in Huehuetenango due to the mountainous and shaded terroir. This means the coee is dried on roof tops, small patios and on tarps. 100% recycle\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003c\/div\u003e\n\u003c\/div\u003e\n\u003c\/div\u003e","published_at":"2026-05-18T11:44:33+02:00","created_at":"2026-01-23T09:36:00+02:00","updated_at":"2026-09-08T20:34:37+02:00","vendor":"Sorcery Coffee Roasters","product_type":"","tags":[],"variants":[{"id":44767886999586,"title":"500G","option1":"500G","option2":null,"option3":null,"sku":null,"requires_shipping":true,"taxable":true,"featured_image":null,"available":true,"price":"369.00","grams":0,"compare_at_price":null,"position":1,"product_id":8209104928802,"created_at":"2026-01-23T09:37:10+02:00","updated_at":"2026-09-08T20:34:37+02:00"},{"id":46534190366754,"title":"1KG","option1":"1KG","option2":null,"option3":null,"sku":null,"requires_shipping":true,"taxable":true,"featured_image":null,"available":true,"price":"550.00","grams":0,"compare_at_price":null,"position":2,"product_id":8209104928802,"created_at":"2026-08-24T08:57:16+02:00","updated_at":"2026-09-08T20:34:37+02:00"}],"images":[{"id":35274498670626,"created_at":"2025-05-14T09:24:50+02:00","position":1,"updated_at":"2025-05-14T09:24:52+02:00","product_id":8209104928802,"variant_ids":[],"src":"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0570\/5138\/1794\/files\/WolishoNew-10.jpg?v=1747207492","width":37